1
00:00:00,201 --> 00:00:06,009
[A Bona Fide Killer]

2
00:00:08,013 --> 00:00:09,013
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

3
00:00:09,013 --> 00:00:10,013
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

4
00:00:10,013 --> 00:00:11,013
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

5
00:00:11,708 --> 00:00:14,110
[Episode 12]

6
00:00:23,916 --> 00:00:25,964
Hang on tight.

7
00:00:25,964 --> 00:00:29,115
If you fall, you'll wreck your feet.

8
00:00:57,980 --> 00:00:59,952
Hey, Bong Tae Min.

9
00:00:59,952 --> 00:01:01,864
Give me that thing from last time.

10
00:01:01,864 --> 00:01:03,072
What thing?

11
00:01:03,072 --> 00:01:04,872
The gun you made.

12
00:01:04,872 --> 00:01:06,581
A gun?

13
00:01:11,855 --> 00:01:12,475
[Deamokjang Milk]

14
00:01:28,624 --> 00:01:30,324
Oh.

15
00:01:31,532 --> 00:01:33,915
You have good hearing.

16
00:01:33,915 --> 00:01:35,848
What are you doing here all by yourself?

17
00:01:38,680 --> 00:01:40,004
I'm practicing.

18
00:01:40,004 --> 00:01:42,128
I want to get revenge when I grow up.

19
00:01:42,128 --> 00:01:43,996
Revenge?

20
00:01:43,996 --> 00:01:45,228
On whom?

21
00:01:45,228 --> 00:01:46,856
Bad adults.

22
00:01:46,856 --> 00:01:51,481
That's not revenge.
It's called punishing the guilty.

23
00:01:54,515 --> 00:01:58,580
You should target their weakest point.

24
00:01:58,580 --> 00:02:00,280
In one shot.

25
00:02:01,056 --> 00:02:02,815
Right on target.

26
00:02:11,940 --> 00:02:15,048
Oh, impressive.

27
00:02:16,396 --> 00:02:19,252
Brave little girl, what's your name?

28
00:02:19,252 --> 00:02:20,904
I'm Yoo Bo Na.

29
00:02:20,904 --> 00:02:22,564
Ma'am, who are you?

30
00:02:22,564 --> 00:02:25,615
Well, who should I say I am?

31
00:02:35,576 --> 00:02:37,276
What is it?

32
00:02:43,112 --> 00:02:44,812
Get inside!

33
00:02:46,844 --> 00:02:48,544
You little...

34
00:02:52,880 --> 00:02:57,381
Kids who bite the hand that feeds
and shelters them

35
00:02:57,381 --> 00:03:00,956
ought to have their lights snuffed out,
don't you think?

36
00:03:03,304 --> 00:03:04,472
Look at this little punk.

37
00:03:04,472 --> 00:03:05,883
What are you going to do with that?

38
00:03:05,883 --> 00:03:07,681
Play with me?

39
00:03:11,928 --> 00:03:13,628
Hey!

40
00:03:16,644 --> 00:03:20,015
<i>What? Why are you doing this to me?</i>

41
00:03:38,504 --> 00:03:40,088
<i>All patrol units, attention.</i>

42
00:03:40,088 --> 00:03:42,312
<i>Right outside Ji Hye Pub in downtown
Iseong-dong, Myeongin-gu.</i>

43
00:03:42,312 --> 00:03:44,396
<i>A drunken man has smashed a soju bottle</i>

44
00:03:44,396 --> 00:03:46,756
<i>and is causing a disturbance,
holding a woman hostage.</i>

45
00:03:46,756 --> 00:03:49,915
- <i>Nearby patrol cars, dispatch now.</i>
- Iseong-dong is right next door.

46
00:03:51,144 --> 00:03:53,060
<i>There are currently no available patrol cars.</i>

47
00:03:53,060 --> 00:03:55,084
<i>Including nearby detectives and mobile units,</i>

48
00:03:55,084 --> 00:03:56,604
<i>all available units, please respond.</i>

49
00:03:56,604 --> 00:03:59,615
Oh, looks like there aren't
any patrol cars nearby.

50
00:04:00,780 --> 00:04:02,240
<i>The situation at the scene is escalating.</i>

51
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:05,908
<i>Nearest available unit, regardless of
assignment, respond immediately.</i>

52
00:04:05,908 --> 00:04:07,842
- Hey, Beom, let's roll.
- Alright.

53
00:04:07,842 --> 00:04:08,920
Two detectives from the Nambu Police Station,

54
00:04:08,920 --> 00:04:11,615
currently staking out near Iseong-dong,
are responding to the scene.

55
00:04:29,268 --> 00:04:32,508
<i>Ms. Bo Na, please stop!</i>

56
00:04:32,508 --> 00:04:34,968
He's already unconscious, Ms. Yoo!

57
00:04:34,968 --> 00:04:36,668
Ms. Yoo!

58
00:04:40,844 --> 00:04:42,776
Yoo Bo Na.

59
00:04:42,776 --> 00:04:44,515
<i>Stop it now.</i>

60
00:04:47,976 --> 00:04:49,681
Director Yoo.

61
00:04:50,879 --> 00:04:52,781
Are you okay?

62
00:05:04,932 --> 00:05:07,515
Did you really not report
a drunken disturbance?

63
00:05:07,515 --> 00:05:09,320
A drunken disturbance?

64
00:05:09,320 --> 00:05:11,681
I never made such a report.

65
00:05:11,681 --> 00:05:12,681
What?

66
00:05:12,681 --> 00:05:18,076
Wait. Didn't a drunk man smash
a soju bottle and threaten a woman?

67
00:05:18,076 --> 00:05:20,328
No. Nothing like that happened.

68
00:05:20,328 --> 00:05:23,081
Are you sure you have the right place?

69
00:05:29,696 --> 00:05:31,415
Darn it.

70
00:05:32,468 --> 00:05:34,381
<i>We've got a witness.</i>

71
00:05:35,424 --> 00:05:38,415
Why is a child who should be
in protective care even here?

72
00:06:03,228 --> 00:06:06,148
Are you okay? Are you hurt anywhere?

73
00:06:07,908 --> 00:06:11,864
We're here to help you out.

74
00:06:11,864 --> 00:06:14,808
Get a good night's sleep.

75
00:06:14,808 --> 00:06:17,781
Tomorrow will be a new day.

76
00:06:40,249 --> 00:06:42,052
<i>Someone has collapsed and is bleeding
from the head on the fifth floor</i>

77
00:06:42,052 --> 00:06:44,652
<i>of the emergency stairs at King Tower.</i>

78
00:06:44,652 --> 00:06:46,881
<i>I think he's going to die
if you don't get here quickly.</i>

79
00:06:52,857 --> 00:06:54,308
Excuse me!

80
00:06:54,308 --> 00:06:57,208
Have we met before?

81
00:06:57,208 --> 00:06:58,856
No.

82
00:06:58,856 --> 00:07:02,081
Oh, it's dangerous
to touch it that carelessly...

83
00:07:05,352 --> 00:07:07,288
How was your first day back at work?
Was it tough?

84
00:07:07,288 --> 00:07:09,781
It's something I've done for a long time,
so it came back quickly.

85
00:07:09,781 --> 00:07:13,628
<i>Some speculate that Kingfisher,
the infamous serial gun killer</i>

86
00:07:13,628 --> 00:07:15,132
<i>who disappeared for the past four years...</i>

87
00:07:15,132 --> 00:07:17,356
Didn't you have a client meeting today?
Did it not go well?

88
00:07:17,356 --> 00:07:21,164
Oh, the meeting fell through this afternoon,
so it got pushed to tonight.

89
00:07:21,164 --> 00:07:22,781
[Kingfisher Strikes Again]
<i>This is the first time</i>

90
00:07:22,781 --> 00:07:25,015
[Two Casino VIP Guests Killed]
<i>two people have been killed</i>

91
00:07:25,015 --> 00:07:27,468
<i>in a single Kingfisher case.</i>

92
00:07:27,468 --> 00:07:29,344
<i>I like you, Bo Na.</i>

93
00:07:29,344 --> 00:07:32,215
You don't really know much about me, do you?

94
00:08:35,396 --> 00:08:37,096
Gu Jong Ryeol!

95
00:08:39,864 --> 00:08:42,648
What? Has someone already called it in?

96
00:08:50,676 --> 00:08:53,060
I'm Detective Lee Dong Jin
from Nambu Station. What's going on?

97
00:08:53,060 --> 00:08:55,748
We received a report that
a sick child is home alone.

98
00:08:55,748 --> 00:08:57,448
I believe this is the house.

99
00:09:05,804 --> 00:09:09,360
For the seven years my dad was in prison,

100
00:09:09,360 --> 00:09:13,420
everyone at school
called me an idiot or a freak.

101
00:09:13,420 --> 00:09:16,056
I was always spaced out.

102
00:09:16,056 --> 00:09:20,715
Even the slightest sound,
like a pen dropping, would make me jump.

103
00:09:21,928 --> 00:09:24,580
<i>If someone even brushed past my shoulder,</i>

104
00:09:24,580 --> 00:09:27,148
I'd collapse and tremble.

105
00:09:28,660 --> 00:09:33,336
The doctors said I'd be fine
and get better with time,

106
00:09:33,336 --> 00:09:35,415
but I never did.

107
00:09:36,316 --> 00:09:38,815
One day, I realized why.

108
00:09:40,092 --> 00:09:41,792
Because Dad would be...

109
00:09:42,952 --> 00:09:45,115
coming back in a few years.

110
00:09:46,556 --> 00:09:49,315
Because it wasn't over yet.

111
00:09:50,348 --> 00:09:54,281
When I watched my dad disappear
right before my eyes,

112
00:09:54,924 --> 00:09:56,748
<i>I thought to myself.</i>

113
00:09:58,804 --> 00:10:00,815
<i>"It's finally over."</i>

114
00:10:03,128 --> 00:10:05,481
<i>"Maybe now I can live...</i>

115
00:10:07,581 --> 00:10:10,008
<i>a normal life,</i>

116
00:10:10,008 --> 00:10:12,081
like everyone else."

117
00:10:13,068 --> 00:10:16,115
Today will probably be
that kind of day for that girl.

118
00:10:17,684 --> 00:10:19,915
The day she's freed from violence.

119
00:10:38,360 --> 00:10:39,603
Save me.

120
00:10:39,603 --> 00:10:43,068
Well... Ugh...

121
00:10:43,068 --> 00:10:45,108
The inhaler... The...

122
00:10:45,108 --> 00:10:47,415
The inhaler... My inhaler, please.

123
00:10:47,415 --> 00:10:48,868
The inhaler...

124
00:10:48,868 --> 00:10:50,681
Please, the inhaler...

125
00:10:53,908 --> 00:10:57,032
Please... Please save me...

126
00:10:57,032 --> 00:10:58,781
Save me. Save...

127
00:11:09,468 --> 00:11:13,181
I'm so sorry I got here so late.

128
00:11:18,564 --> 00:11:21,848
I'll take care of the rest.

129
00:11:45,515 --> 00:11:50,108
Your friends will all go somewhere safe.

130
00:11:50,108 --> 00:11:52,384
You're the one who saved those children.

131
00:11:52,384 --> 00:11:55,081
<i>The reason I do this work.</i>

132
00:12:12,520 --> 00:12:15,048
<i>I hope at least one person can be saved,</i>

133
00:12:15,856 --> 00:12:19,881
<i>and someone can be safe because of it.</i>

134
00:12:54,716 --> 00:12:56,416
Tae Seong.

135
00:13:07,376 --> 00:13:09,076
Honey.

136
00:13:10,308 --> 00:13:12,008
Tae Seong.

137
00:13:21,701 --> 00:13:23,156
<i>Hello?</i>

138
00:13:23,156 --> 00:13:25,948
Where are you now, Tae Seong?

139
00:13:32,901 --> 00:13:34,601
Honey!

140
00:13:38,252 --> 00:13:39,952
Yul!

141
00:13:40,564 --> 00:13:43,148
What's wrong with Yul? Huh?

142
00:13:44,828 --> 00:13:46,972
Her fever suddenly spiked
while she was sleeping.

143
00:13:46,972 --> 00:13:49,172
They say it's the fever cold
that's been going around lately.

144
00:13:49,172 --> 00:13:52,396
A cold? She was fine this morning. How did...

145
00:13:52,396 --> 00:13:56,680
So did they say she'll be okay? Huh? Huh?

146
00:13:56,680 --> 00:14:00,004
Her fever broke. They said to monitor her
for a day or two with medication.

147
00:14:00,004 --> 00:14:03,156
She's so tiny, and now...

148
00:14:03,156 --> 00:14:06,248
Yul, you must've been in so much pain, huh?

149
00:14:08,524 --> 00:14:10,880
Oh, poor baby, Yul.

150
00:14:10,880 --> 00:14:13,960
Oh, no, you must've been hurting so much.

151
00:14:13,960 --> 00:14:16,148
Oh, they had to put that
on such a little kid...

152
00:14:18,215 --> 00:14:22,415
Oh, no. I'm sorry Mommy got here so late.

153
00:14:43,388 --> 00:14:46,981
I'll stay by Yul's side tonight.
You go get some rest.

154
00:14:50,680 --> 00:14:54,715
I'll take the day off tomorrow
and stay with Yul, honey.

155
00:14:56,124 --> 00:14:57,824
Okay, then.

156
00:15:08,192 --> 00:15:11,747
[Yul's Room]

157
00:16:02,198 --> 00:16:03,798
[Breaking News: Child Abuser
Gu Jong Ryeol Found Dead Last Night]

158
00:16:10,032 --> 00:16:11,732
Last night...

159
00:16:14,548 --> 00:16:16,878
[Big Precious]

160
00:16:24,991 --> 00:16:26,787
[Big Precious]

161
00:16:46,736 --> 00:16:48,912
[Big Precious]
<i>Honey, when did you leave?</i>

162
00:16:48,912 --> 00:16:50,660
<i>You should've woken me.</i>

163
00:16:50,660 --> 00:16:53,340
<i>I would've made you some toast.</i>

164
00:16:53,340 --> 00:16:55,740
<i>Did you take your umbrella?</i>

165
00:16:55,740 --> 00:16:57,973
<i>My husband can't get caught in the rain.</i>

166
00:16:57,973 --> 00:16:59,733
Oh, my...

167
00:17:19,228 --> 00:17:24,528
It seems there are still a lot of things
you don't know about Bo Na.

168
00:17:24,528 --> 00:17:25,828
Oh.

169
00:17:25,828 --> 00:17:28,315
Or does she just not tell you
much about herself?

170
00:17:31,864 --> 00:17:34,948
Yes, Manager Kim. I'm Kwon Tae Seong,
a reporter from Not Today.

171
00:17:34,948 --> 00:17:37,148
Hello. How have you been?

172
00:17:37,496 --> 00:17:38,840
[Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency]

173
00:17:38,840 --> 00:17:43,260
This case is definitely different
from the pattern we've seen so far.

174
00:17:43,260 --> 00:17:47,520
It's the first time we've found evidence
that the killer physically intervened.

175
00:17:47,520 --> 00:17:51,324
The use of violence suggests
some emotion was involved.

176
00:17:51,324 --> 00:17:54,784
Well, the more enraged you are,
the more times you tend to stab someone.

177
00:17:54,784 --> 00:17:57,348
The fact that they called
an ambulance to report a sick child

178
00:17:57,348 --> 00:18:00,536
also shows that even amid all those emotions,

179
00:18:00,536 --> 00:18:03,215
they clearly wanted to protect the child.

180
00:18:04,232 --> 00:18:06,592
Which means...

181
00:18:06,592 --> 00:18:09,892
What is this, a funeral? Why the long faces?

182
00:18:09,892 --> 00:18:11,781
- Welcome, sir.
- Welcome, sir.

183
00:18:13,191 --> 00:18:16,323
I'm sorry. I should've been more careful.

184
00:18:16,323 --> 00:18:18,212
I let my guard down.

185
00:18:18,212 --> 00:18:19,404
What are you sorry for?

186
00:18:19,404 --> 00:18:22,515
Anyway, we've confirmed that
your theory was right.

187
00:18:22,515 --> 00:18:23,515
Haven't we?

188
00:18:23,515 --> 00:18:25,581
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, that's right.

189
00:18:27,079 --> 00:18:28,007
[Lee Dong Jin]

190
00:18:28,336 --> 00:18:32,924
Don't get down just because Kingfisher
got away this time. Keep at it.

191
00:18:32,924 --> 00:18:36,128
Next time, I'll get the chief to give us
all the support we need,

192
00:18:36,128 --> 00:18:37,676
even if I have to beg him for it.

193
00:18:37,676 --> 00:18:39,434
Got it?

194
00:18:39,434 --> 00:18:40,434
Got it?

195
00:18:40,434 --> 00:18:42,315
- Yes, sir.
- Understood, sir.

196
00:18:44,028 --> 00:18:45,032
You haven't had lunch, right?

197
00:18:45,032 --> 00:18:47,748
Use the department credit card
and treat yourself to something nice.

198
00:18:49,048 --> 00:18:51,012
Answer me.

199
00:18:51,012 --> 00:18:53,220
- We'll enjoy it.
- Thank you, sir.

200
00:18:53,220 --> 00:18:56,548
I expected him to be strict,
but he's actually pretty chill.

201
00:18:58,276 --> 00:19:00,616
He's been part of the task force
two times before.

202
00:19:00,616 --> 00:19:02,848
Both times, it ended badly,
and he was furious about it.

203
00:19:02,848 --> 00:19:06,515
He's probably the one among us
who wants to catch Kingfisher the most.

204
00:19:06,755 --> 00:19:08,047
[Team Leader Gu Tae Seok]

205
00:19:10,681 --> 00:19:13,420
<i>But there's one thing
that doesn't quite add up.</i>

206
00:19:13,420 --> 00:19:15,612
The false dispatch order
that came into the scene.

207
00:19:15,612 --> 00:19:17,260
We sent it to the voice analysis team,

208
00:19:17,260 --> 00:19:20,972
and they say it was AI-generated,
not a real person's voice.

209
00:19:20,972 --> 00:19:24,564
It looks like our police network was hacked.

210
00:19:24,564 --> 00:19:26,616
Hacked?

211
00:19:26,616 --> 00:19:27,904
What does that mean, then?

212
00:19:27,904 --> 00:19:31,015
Did they know we were coming and diverted us?

213
00:19:31,015 --> 00:19:32,988
How?

214
00:19:32,988 --> 00:19:37,276
Could there be a Kingfisher operative
inside the police?

215
00:19:37,276 --> 00:19:40,081
You know, like an undercover operative.

216
00:19:41,616 --> 00:19:45,868
[The Kingfisher Case Files]
<i>It doesn't have to be someone in the police.</i>

217
00:19:45,868 --> 00:19:48,000
<i>I heard Kingfisher's fan cafe alone</i>

218
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:51,048
<i>has over a million members, right?</i>

219
00:19:57,140 --> 00:20:00,248
<i>Should prison</i>

220
00:20:00,248 --> 00:20:03,856
be a hideout for criminals? Huh?

221
00:20:03,856 --> 00:20:09,328
We're already overcrowded as it is,
running out of space,

222
00:20:09,328 --> 00:20:11,081
aren't we?

223
00:20:13,832 --> 00:20:15,140
<i>Who knows?</i>

224
00:20:15,140 --> 00:20:16,681
<i>Among them could be someone
consumed by vengeance</i>

225
00:20:16,681 --> 00:20:19,115
[Durumi Electronics]
<i>after losing family to a criminal.</i>

226
00:20:22,628 --> 00:20:24,456
<i>Maybe...</i>

227
00:20:24,456 --> 00:20:27,715
<i>helpers like that are hiding in places
we never see.</i>

228
00:20:27,739 --> 00:20:28,732
[No Entry to Above-Ground Parking]

229
00:20:34,048 --> 00:20:35,592
Oh, wow!

230
00:20:35,592 --> 00:20:37,988
Wow, it's green!

231
00:20:37,988 --> 00:20:42,096
It's done. Once you finish your porridge,
you'll feel better in no time, right?

232
00:20:42,096 --> 00:20:44,596
Yeah, I'll eat lots.

233
00:20:44,596 --> 00:20:47,248
You will? Eat plenty.

234
00:20:54,644 --> 00:20:56,656
Did it hurt when you got the shot?

235
00:20:56,656 --> 00:20:58,560
Yeah, it hurt.

236
00:20:58,560 --> 00:21:00,908
But Daddy hugged me tight.

237
00:21:00,908 --> 00:21:02,268
He did?

238
00:21:02,268 --> 00:21:05,576
Yul, were you sad because Mommy wasn't there?

239
00:21:05,576 --> 00:21:08,592
Yeah, I cried because I missed you.

240
00:21:08,592 --> 00:21:12,515
I asked Daddy to call you, but he wouldn't.

241
00:21:13,744 --> 00:21:15,496
He did?

242
00:21:15,496 --> 00:21:16,496
Why would Daddy do that?

243
00:21:16,496 --> 00:21:17,612
I don't know.

244
00:21:17,612 --> 00:21:19,312
Eat up.

245
00:22:06,648 --> 00:22:08,848
Back then...

246
00:22:08,848 --> 00:22:11,248
the person who was on the rooftop
beyond that door...

247
00:22:14,816 --> 00:22:16,615
was it Yoo Bo Na?

248
00:22:17,700 --> 00:22:21,415
Looks like you didn't sleep.
Your face looks haggard.

249
00:22:22,308 --> 00:22:25,015
The person you tried to hide that day...

250
00:22:27,856 --> 00:22:29,781
was it Yoo Bo Na?

251
00:22:32,388 --> 00:22:34,088
Good grief.

252
00:22:35,364 --> 00:22:39,081
Why are you walking around in the rain?
You'll catch a cold.

253
00:22:50,284 --> 00:22:53,015
So you finally opened the door.

254
00:22:59,336 --> 00:23:01,624
But that's strange.

255
00:23:01,624 --> 00:23:03,992
Why come to me and ask about it?

256
00:23:03,992 --> 00:23:05,881
The person involved is right there.

257
00:23:07,681 --> 00:23:11,515
Were you afraid she'd kill you if you asked?

258
00:23:14,664 --> 00:23:16,364
Are you upset?

259
00:23:17,581 --> 00:23:21,172
Well, I suppose you have
every right to be angry.

260
00:23:21,172 --> 00:23:26,056
After all those years of marriage,
she completely deceived her own husband.

261
00:23:26,056 --> 00:23:29,015
And she hid such a terrifying secret.

262
00:23:30,715 --> 00:23:33,708
That's just how Yoo Bo Na is.

263
00:23:33,708 --> 00:23:37,500
She's that meticulous and shrewd.

264
00:23:37,500 --> 00:23:42,292
She wouldn't even bat an eye
at making a fool out of someone.

265
00:23:42,292 --> 00:23:43,992
Shut up.

266
00:23:45,720 --> 00:23:49,044
I'm taking your side right now,
Mr. Kwon Tae Seong.

267
00:23:49,044 --> 00:23:51,815
What do you know to be talking like that?

268
00:23:53,015 --> 00:23:56,648
Say one more thing like that,
and I won't let you off.

269
00:24:31,160 --> 00:24:33,848
I heard the child was
in a protective shelter.

270
00:24:33,848 --> 00:24:35,896
What happened yesterday?

271
00:24:35,896 --> 00:24:41,144
We have no choice but to release
a child when the parents request it.

272
00:24:41,144 --> 00:24:44,200
At the time, the adoptive mom
was considered the main culprit,

273
00:24:44,200 --> 00:24:47,484
so we had no grounds
to deny the dad's request.

274
00:24:47,484 --> 00:24:52,456
Would it be possible for us
to speak with the child?

275
00:24:52,456 --> 00:24:55,560
I'm sorry, but I'm afraid
that's not possible.

276
00:24:55,560 --> 00:24:58,232
The child's doctor stressed that

277
00:24:58,232 --> 00:25:00,824
her physical and emotional
well-being has to come first.

278
00:25:00,824 --> 00:25:02,524
I see.

279
00:25:10,560 --> 00:25:14,815
So that punk was abusing
the child again all that time.

280
00:25:16,032 --> 00:25:18,532
Could Kingfisher
have witnessed the abuse live?

281
00:25:18,532 --> 00:25:20,976
Could that be why he beat him so brutally?
He saw it and lost his temper?

282
00:25:20,976 --> 00:25:23,081
It's possible.

283
00:25:23,081 --> 00:25:26,028
Oh, then the kid must've seen something.

284
00:25:26,028 --> 00:25:29,620
If you were her, would you tell us?

285
00:25:29,620 --> 00:25:31,548
Actually, I wouldn't either.

286
00:25:31,548 --> 00:25:34,156
He saved her life. She'd owe him
for the rest of her life.

287
00:25:34,156 --> 00:25:35,781
You said that other kid
didn't say anything either.

288
00:25:35,781 --> 00:25:37,848
The one whose dad died on Christmas.

289
00:25:39,952 --> 00:25:41,615
<i>The daughter's name was 'Oh' something.</i>

290
00:25:41,615 --> 00:25:43,315
Wait a second.

291
00:25:45,664 --> 00:25:47,364
Oh Seung Ah.

292
00:25:48,815 --> 00:25:50,912
Let's look for Oh Seung Ah.

293
00:25:50,912 --> 00:25:53,415
What? Her?

294
00:25:53,415 --> 00:25:55,181
So far, there have been exactly

295
00:25:55,181 --> 00:25:58,068
two people at Kingfisher
crime scenes who weren't victims.

296
00:25:58,068 --> 00:25:59,912
Yeon Chang Bok's son must still be young.

297
00:25:59,912 --> 00:26:02,152
And Oh Seung Ah would be an adult by now.

298
00:26:02,152 --> 00:26:03,796
Who knows?

299
00:26:03,796 --> 00:26:07,008
As you said, maybe she's repaying
Kingfisher for saving her.

300
00:26:07,008 --> 00:26:08,288
Let's find her.

301
00:26:08,288 --> 00:26:10,981
Oh, genius!

302
00:26:16,060 --> 00:26:18,128
- Hey!
- Oh, you're here?

303
00:26:18,128 --> 00:26:19,728
Oh, I'm exhausted.

304
00:26:19,728 --> 00:26:22,181
Hey, he's pretty drunk.

305
00:26:28,268 --> 00:26:30,015
Reporter Kwon Tae Seong?

306
00:26:33,348 --> 00:26:37,036
What are you doing here all by yourself,
looking so miserable?

307
00:26:37,036 --> 00:26:38,960
What? Why do you look like a mess?

308
00:26:38,960 --> 00:26:40,315
Reporter Go!

309
00:26:40,315 --> 00:26:44,584
Go Ji Soon! My dear colleague, Go Ji Soon.

310
00:26:44,584 --> 00:26:46,415
- Go Ji Soon!
- Hey, what's wrong with you?

311
00:26:46,415 --> 00:26:48,348
- Go Ji Soon!
- Sit down. Sit down.

312
00:26:48,348 --> 00:26:51,024
Hey, the Chief is really mad.

313
00:26:51,024 --> 00:26:54,492
Hey, you always turned me down
when I asked you to drink,

314
00:26:54,492 --> 00:26:56,364
saying you missed your wife, huh?

315
00:26:56,364 --> 00:27:00,315
And now you're drinking all by yourself?

316
00:27:02,148 --> 00:27:04,081
Did you two have a marital spat?

317
00:27:06,556 --> 00:27:08,648
What's that?

318
00:27:10,048 --> 00:27:12,568
How do you even have one?

319
00:27:12,568 --> 00:27:14,115
You're annoying.

320
00:27:14,115 --> 00:27:16,204
Oh, you're so annoying.

321
00:27:16,204 --> 00:27:20,448
Hey, do you really love your wife that much?

322
00:27:24,144 --> 00:27:25,712
- I do.
- What do you like about her?

323
00:27:25,712 --> 00:27:28,732
What's so great about her?

324
00:27:28,732 --> 00:27:30,815
My wife

325
00:27:30,815 --> 00:27:35,581
can climb rough mountain trails
like it's nothing.

326
00:27:35,581 --> 00:27:38,648
Even when the snow stacks up
as tall as you are,

327
00:27:38,648 --> 00:27:41,809
she plows through like an excavator.

328
00:27:41,809 --> 00:27:47,920
And she's incredibly strong,
so she can lift me right off the ground.

329
00:27:47,920 --> 00:27:51,784
And she's a great shot.

330
00:27:51,784 --> 00:27:54,415
She's not your wife. She's a superhero.

331
00:28:00,448 --> 00:28:03,915
It was our first date in Seoul.

332
00:28:05,616 --> 00:28:08,815
When I asked where she wanted to go,

333
00:28:08,815 --> 00:28:14,115
she just wanted to eat tteokbokki
on the street and buy a hair tie.

334
00:28:14,828 --> 00:28:19,681
When I asked why she
wanted to do those things,

335
00:28:19,681 --> 00:28:23,268
she said she just wanted to
experience those ordinary things.

336
00:28:23,268 --> 00:28:25,556
What kind of cheesy story is that?

337
00:28:25,556 --> 00:28:27,848
When she was pregnant with Yul,

338
00:28:28,796 --> 00:28:30,540
she had really bad morning sickness.

339
00:28:30,540 --> 00:28:32,681
So after work every day,

340
00:28:32,681 --> 00:28:36,015
I got some strawberries
and mixed them with ice for her.

341
00:28:36,748 --> 00:28:40,272
My wife really loves strawberry shakes.

342
00:28:40,272 --> 00:28:42,136
Do you know what she said to me once?

343
00:28:42,136 --> 00:28:44,240
What?

344
00:28:44,240 --> 00:28:46,915
"At this rate, am I going to
give birth to a strawberry?"

345
00:28:50,624 --> 00:28:52,324
Isn't that funny?

346
00:28:54,196 --> 00:28:58,281
Man, you're really rubbing salt
in this old bachelor's wounds.

347
00:29:00,064 --> 00:29:02,144
So?

348
00:29:02,144 --> 00:29:03,844
Are you happy?

349
00:29:06,916 --> 00:29:08,616
I am.

350
00:29:10,080 --> 00:29:12,848
I'm so happy that I could go crazy.

351
00:29:14,760 --> 00:29:16,748
Jeez.

352
00:29:21,648 --> 00:29:23,840
Where are you going?

353
00:29:23,840 --> 00:29:25,648
To see my wife.

354
00:29:43,980 --> 00:29:45,680
You're back?

355
00:29:46,980 --> 00:29:50,415
Why'd you drink so much? Huh?

356
00:30:04,504 --> 00:30:06,204
Well...

357
00:30:08,516 --> 00:30:10,881
I'll get you some honey water, honey.

358
00:30:16,152 --> 00:30:18,815
Honey, drink this. It's honey water.

359
00:30:19,476 --> 00:30:21,176
Okay?

360
00:30:22,628 --> 00:30:24,872
We're married, right?

361
00:30:24,872 --> 00:30:27,204
Of course, we are.

362
00:30:27,204 --> 00:30:29,500
Drink this and sober up a little.

363
00:30:29,500 --> 00:30:33,748
You're my wife, and I'm your husband.

364
00:30:35,372 --> 00:30:38,715
You're Yul's mom, and I'm Yul's dad.

365
00:30:40,152 --> 00:30:41,852
That's what it is.

366
00:30:46,644 --> 00:30:48,344
Right?

367
00:30:51,388 --> 00:30:54,115
Honey, did something happen today?

368
00:30:54,115 --> 00:30:57,181
You haven't answered your phone all day.
What's wrong?

369
00:31:03,628 --> 00:31:06,154
I'm asking because I'm genuinely curious.

370
00:31:06,154 --> 00:31:08,581
Please give me an honest answer.

371
00:31:09,766 --> 00:31:11,432
Okay.

372
00:31:11,432 --> 00:31:13,681
What do you want to know?

373
00:31:13,681 --> 00:31:15,381
Do you...

374
00:31:18,484 --> 00:31:21,948
Do you really like strawberry shakes?

375
00:31:24,764 --> 00:31:26,815
Is that really true?

376
00:31:31,048 --> 00:31:32,948
Are you really Yoo Bo Na...

377
00:31:33,784 --> 00:31:37,481
You are, right?
You're really Yoo Bo Na, right?

378
00:31:41,232 --> 00:31:44,381
You seem really drunk. Let's go to bed.

379
00:31:48,584 --> 00:31:50,781
What am I to you?

380
00:31:53,040 --> 00:31:56,236
Are you angry with me about something, honey?

381
00:31:56,236 --> 00:32:00,815
Is this because I came home late
without calling yesterday?

382
00:32:00,815 --> 00:32:02,948
Why did you marry me?

383
00:32:08,648 --> 00:32:10,781
Did you really love me?

384
00:33:07,560 --> 00:33:11,415
I actually don't really like
strawberry shakes.

385
00:33:12,452 --> 00:33:14,152
They're too cold.

386
00:33:14,956 --> 00:33:20,115
But when I fell in love,
I really wanted to do that.

387
00:33:21,015 --> 00:33:23,915
Sitting across from each other
and drinking strawberry shakes.

388
00:33:27,160 --> 00:33:29,815
So I just pretended to like them.

389
00:33:32,584 --> 00:33:35,848
Because I wanted to keep doing that with you.

390
00:33:37,652 --> 00:33:41,015
I just loved those moments so much.

391
00:33:44,932 --> 00:33:47,681
Because that's the kind of
person you are to me.

392
00:35:08,100 --> 00:35:10,448
Hey, stop right there!

393
00:35:12,100 --> 00:35:13,800
Oh, there you go again.

394
00:35:15,780 --> 00:35:17,480
What is it?

395
00:35:19,644 --> 00:35:21,920
<i>Have you eaten?</i>

396
00:35:21,920 --> 00:35:24,448
<i>You didn't just snack your way
through another meal, did you?</i>

397
00:35:28,881 --> 00:35:33,015
<i>I ate! Two full bowls of rice
with kimchi stew.</i>

398
00:35:34,076 --> 00:35:35,584
<i>Good job.</i>

399
00:35:35,584 --> 00:35:37,881
<i>Make sure you eat dinner too.</i>

400
00:35:41,796 --> 00:35:42,848
<i>Kwon Se Ah.</i>

401
00:35:42,848 --> 00:35:45,348
I really do like you,

402
00:35:45,348 --> 00:35:47,881
and I was a little upset that
I couldn't see you.

403
00:35:47,881 --> 00:35:51,615
So I'd like you to reply when I text you.

404
00:35:55,028 --> 00:35:57,081
<i>Have you eaten? Eat real food, not ramyeon.</i>

405
00:35:57,081 --> 00:35:58,156
<i>I ate!</i>

406
00:35:58,156 --> 00:35:59,680
<i>Good. What did you eat for lunch?</i>

407
00:35:59,680 --> 00:36:01,148
<i>I mixed tuna with rice.</i>

408
00:36:01,148 --> 00:36:02,972
<i>Oh, sounds good. I'm having dinner.</i>

409
00:36:02,972 --> 00:36:04,715
<i>Have you eaten? Enjoy your meal.</i>

410
00:36:04,715 --> 00:36:07,516
Why are you doing this to me?

411
00:36:07,516 --> 00:36:09,532
Is this the only reason
you asked me to respond?

412
00:36:09,532 --> 00:36:12,515
Are you like a meal-tracking robot or what?

413
00:36:13,548 --> 00:36:14,915
Oh, come on!

414
00:36:14,915 --> 00:36:17,848
I've already eaten! Quit it!

415
00:36:17,848 --> 00:36:19,936
<i>Se Ah, what are you doing tomorrow?</i>

416
00:36:19,936 --> 00:36:22,548
- Oh!
- <i>Shall we meet up?</i>

417
00:36:23,215 --> 00:36:25,415
<i>Is there anywhere you'd like to go?</i>

418
00:36:25,415 --> 00:36:27,848
Yes, yes, yes!

419
00:36:33,800 --> 00:36:35,108
Wow, they're so pretty.

420
00:36:35,108 --> 00:36:36,488
Hello!

421
00:36:36,488 --> 00:36:38,715
Look at its eyes. So pretty.

422
00:36:38,715 --> 00:36:40,115
Come here.

423
00:36:40,115 --> 00:36:42,140
Hello.

424
00:36:42,140 --> 00:36:48,128
Because horses evolved
while being chased by predators,

425
00:36:48,128 --> 00:36:52,052
they can be extremely sensitive to
unfamiliar environments or sudden stimuli...

426
00:36:52,052 --> 00:36:53,772
Let's give it a try, okay?

427
00:36:53,772 --> 00:36:56,300
Sir, can we ride this?

428
00:36:56,300 --> 00:36:59,104
I've never ridden anything except in a car...

429
00:36:59,104 --> 00:37:00,848
Se Ah!

430
00:37:00,848 --> 00:37:02,740
Up you go.

431
00:37:02,740 --> 00:37:04,740
Wow, it's really high.

432
00:37:04,740 --> 00:37:05,976
- Is it fun?
- Yeah.

433
00:37:05,976 --> 00:37:07,515
- Come on, get on.
- No, I'm fine.

434
00:37:07,515 --> 00:37:09,220
He's going to ride too.

435
00:37:09,220 --> 00:37:10,920
I'm fine.

436
00:37:14,740 --> 00:37:17,115
You're... really good at it.

437
00:37:17,872 --> 00:37:19,572
How is it?

438
00:37:23,680 --> 00:37:26,381
- Wow, careful.
- This is amazing.

439
00:37:36,448 --> 00:37:38,560
How did they even ride this?

440
00:37:38,560 --> 00:37:40,848
With the growing emphasis on
low-carbon green growth,

441
00:37:40,848 --> 00:37:43,460
bicycle culture is becoming
increasingly popular...

442
00:37:43,460 --> 00:37:46,581
Wow, let's ride bikes too.

443
00:37:47,415 --> 00:37:49,848
Well, but I've only ever
driven large vehicles...

444
00:37:50,612 --> 00:37:53,252
Assistant Manager Ki, you need to pedal.

445
00:37:53,252 --> 00:37:54,981
Okay?

446
00:37:58,224 --> 00:37:59,981
Fun, right?

447
00:38:03,904 --> 00:38:05,681
It's really nice, right?

448
00:38:15,534 --> 00:38:16,364
[Mr. Tiger]

449
00:38:18,964 --> 00:38:21,648
<i>Did you eat lunch? What'd you have?</i>

450
00:38:22,288 --> 00:38:24,881
<i>I ate jjamppong.</i>

451
00:38:28,588 --> 00:38:31,624
Can I ask you something?

452
00:38:31,624 --> 00:38:32,915
What is it?

453
00:38:32,915 --> 00:38:37,681
What do women like men to say to them?

454
00:38:37,681 --> 00:38:41,856
Something that'll move
a relationship along quickly?

455
00:38:41,856 --> 00:38:43,732
Why bother saying something long?

456
00:38:43,732 --> 00:38:45,948
One sentence is enough.

457
00:38:45,948 --> 00:38:47,648
One sentence?

458
00:38:49,400 --> 00:38:51,196
Ms. Kwon Se Ah.

459
00:38:51,196 --> 00:38:52,460
Yes?

460
00:38:52,460 --> 00:38:54,328
- I love you.
- Yes.

461
00:38:54,328 --> 00:38:56,028
What?

462
00:38:56,848 --> 00:38:59,181
<i>Did I hear that wrong?</i>

463
00:38:59,181 --> 00:39:01,181
You heard me right.

464
00:39:01,912 --> 00:39:03,396
I love you, Se Ah.

465
00:39:03,396 --> 00:39:04,632
What?

466
00:39:04,632 --> 00:39:06,332
Why?

467
00:39:07,076 --> 00:39:09,008
You don't like hearing that?

468
00:39:09,008 --> 00:39:10,496
Oh, no.

469
00:39:10,496 --> 00:39:12,472
It's not that at all. But...

470
00:39:12,472 --> 00:39:14,615
<i>He must be joking, right?</i>

471
00:39:14,615 --> 00:39:16,948
I'm not joking.

472
00:39:16,948 --> 00:39:18,648
I mean it.

473
00:39:25,064 --> 00:39:27,400
By the way, Assistant Manager Ki,
can you read minds or something?

474
00:39:27,400 --> 00:39:31,381
Se Ah, your thoughts
are written all over your face.

475
00:39:31,381 --> 00:39:34,115
That's why I like you even better.

476
00:39:40,596 --> 00:39:42,248
Oh, it's so nice here.

477
00:39:42,248 --> 00:39:45,148
The view is beautiful,
and it's so refreshing.

478
00:39:51,754 --> 00:39:54,397
Yeah.

479
00:40:03,276 --> 00:40:07,652
Why did he suddenly say, "I love you"?

480
00:40:07,652 --> 00:40:09,881
How many times have you even seen me?

481
00:40:11,104 --> 00:40:13,736
Is Assistant Manager Ki the kind of guy
who falls in love right away?

482
00:40:13,736 --> 00:40:16,181
He didn't seem like it, though.

483
00:40:16,181 --> 00:40:18,415
Well, wouldn't people normally say

484
00:40:18,415 --> 00:40:21,276
something like "I like you"

485
00:40:21,276 --> 00:40:27,140
or "Do you want to date me?" first?

486
00:40:27,140 --> 00:40:30,048
Well, I'd have to try it myself to know.

487
00:40:42,408 --> 00:40:44,124
That punk...

488
00:40:44,124 --> 00:40:47,728
Hey! You get a 30,000-won fine
for riding on the sidewalk!

489
00:40:47,728 --> 00:40:49,128
I caught you.

490
00:40:49,128 --> 00:40:51,381
I've seen your face!

491
00:41:16,900 --> 00:41:18,648
Have you eaten?

492
00:41:20,372 --> 00:41:23,560
I ate. Pizza and pasta.

493
00:41:23,560 --> 00:41:25,596
Good job.

494
00:41:25,596 --> 00:41:28,164
Oh, why were you
spacing out like that earlier?

495
00:41:28,164 --> 00:41:29,881
Did something happen?

496
00:41:30,896 --> 00:41:33,981
No, nothing.

497
00:41:36,572 --> 00:41:38,272
Want to go play some games?

498
00:41:39,784 --> 00:41:42,348
- No.
- Want to go get some chicken feet?

499
00:41:44,476 --> 00:41:46,176
No.

500
00:41:46,816 --> 00:41:48,228
Why?

501
00:41:48,228 --> 00:41:49,692
Because I like you?

502
00:41:49,692 --> 00:41:52,644
Hey, don't say things like that.

503
00:41:52,644 --> 00:41:54,448
It's making me uncomfortable.

504
00:42:02,218 --> 00:42:03,918
Kwon Se Ah.

505
00:42:05,760 --> 00:42:07,768
I do like you,

506
00:42:07,768 --> 00:42:10,781
but these are just my feelings.

507
00:42:10,781 --> 00:42:13,748
Of course, I respect
whatever you feel toward me.

508
00:42:13,748 --> 00:42:19,181
The time I've spent with you
and our friendship mean a lot to me.

509
00:42:19,181 --> 00:42:23,015
If you meet someone you like,
I'll let go of my feelings.

510
00:42:24,240 --> 00:42:28,256
Until then, I'll just keep feeling this way.

511
00:42:28,256 --> 00:42:32,015
So can't you just hang out with me today?

512
00:42:33,595 --> 00:42:38,581
Hey, I'd be really hurt if this
made things awkward between us.

513
00:42:42,904 --> 00:42:45,352
Oh, say something.

514
00:42:45,352 --> 00:42:49,181
You have to tell me
what you're thinking for me to know.

515
00:42:55,696 --> 00:42:57,612
Okay.

516
00:42:57,612 --> 00:43:03,115
But if you say something like "I like you"
one more time, I'm going to kill you.

517
00:43:04,004 --> 00:43:05,704
Okay!

518
00:43:07,436 --> 00:43:09,272
Let's go.

519
00:43:09,272 --> 00:43:10,384
Don't do that.

520
00:43:10,384 --> 00:43:11,532
Where? Let's go!

521
00:43:11,532 --> 00:43:12,615
Let's start with the PC bang.

522
00:43:12,615 --> 00:43:14,348
Good.

523
00:43:20,181 --> 00:43:22,384
Oh, Mr. Jo. What's up this early?

524
00:43:22,384 --> 00:43:25,180
Sir, that woman who's your friend's wife...

525
00:43:25,180 --> 00:43:28,520
The one who caught those voice-phishing
scammers herself last time.

526
00:43:28,520 --> 00:43:30,224
<i>What does she do for a living?</i>

527
00:43:30,224 --> 00:43:31,404
Ms. Bo Na?

528
00:43:31,404 --> 00:43:33,368
She's just an ordinary office worker. Why?

529
00:43:33,368 --> 00:43:36,952
Wow. I thought she worked in
action or something.

530
00:43:36,952 --> 00:43:38,472
She's quite the joker, huh?

531
00:43:38,472 --> 00:43:42,220
What those scammers said
about her was actually true?

532
00:43:42,220 --> 00:43:44,048
Just send it over for now.

533
00:43:50,724 --> 00:43:53,208
So he just jumped over those buildings?

534
00:43:53,208 --> 00:43:55,381
What, did he fly?

535
00:43:57,492 --> 00:43:59,896
What a lunatic.

536
00:43:59,896 --> 00:44:02,481
What on earth are you thinking?

537
00:44:27,216 --> 00:44:30,915
Are you finished already?
Or did you not even start?

538
00:44:37,648 --> 00:44:40,832
Why'd you leave your job, Team Leader?

539
00:44:40,832 --> 00:44:43,260
All of a sudden? Come on.

540
00:44:43,260 --> 00:44:45,892
I told you before.

541
00:44:45,892 --> 00:44:48,932
I was exhausted physically and emotionally
after divorcing the kids' dad,

542
00:44:48,932 --> 00:44:50,981
and I lost the will to work.

543
00:44:50,981 --> 00:44:55,548
People change when life takes a major turn.

544
00:44:57,752 --> 00:44:59,748
I didn't believe you back then, either.

545
00:45:01,388 --> 00:45:03,915
But was there really no other reason?

546
00:45:10,044 --> 00:45:12,348
Because my husband found out.

547
00:45:13,516 --> 00:45:15,681
What I was really doing.

548
00:45:16,388 --> 00:45:20,972
He told me to quit immediately
and disappear somewhere far away.

549
00:45:20,972 --> 00:45:24,581
And never show my face
in front of the family again.

550
00:45:25,540 --> 00:45:27,224
In return, he said he'd keep it a secret

551
00:45:27,224 --> 00:45:28,781
from the kids for the rest of their lives.

552
00:45:29,984 --> 00:45:31,868
Sure, I said yes.

553
00:45:31,868 --> 00:45:35,115
What else could I do? I'm their mom.

554
00:45:35,115 --> 00:45:37,415
I have to protect my kids.

555
00:45:41,976 --> 00:45:44,715
Why are you suddenly asking that?

556
00:45:46,060 --> 00:45:48,881
So an unavoidable variable
popped up with your husband, huh?

557
00:45:48,881 --> 00:45:52,181
Is this about him coming by last time?

558
00:45:55,296 --> 00:45:57,281
I'm not sure.

559
00:45:58,180 --> 00:46:00,548
I want to ask, but I can't bring myself to.

560
00:46:04,464 --> 00:46:07,008
You're worrying in advance

561
00:46:07,008 --> 00:46:10,515
because you're afraid of
what the answer might be, right?

562
00:46:15,781 --> 00:46:19,515
Not every story ends the same way.

563
00:46:19,515 --> 00:46:24,015
Besides, he's your husband, and he cares
about you more than anyone else.

564
00:46:24,844 --> 00:46:26,881
That's not like you.

565
00:46:27,580 --> 00:46:30,815
You're not the type to worry in advance.

566
00:46:38,251 --> 00:46:40,078
- Oh, you're here?
- Yeah.

567
00:46:40,078 --> 00:46:43,060
About Oh Seung Ah, you asked me
to look into, she changed her name.

568
00:46:43,060 --> 00:46:44,452
Changed it? To what?

569
00:46:44,452 --> 00:46:45,817
Oh Hyun Nam.

570
00:46:45,817 --> 00:46:47,565
[Personal Information]
This is her current ID photo.

571
00:46:47,565 --> 00:46:49,676
Her current address is
Hanan-ro in Yangpyeong-gu.

572
00:46:49,676 --> 00:46:51,541
And she seems to have a decent job too.

573
00:46:51,541 --> 00:46:52,805
Where does she work?

574
00:46:52,805 --> 00:46:54,852
Durumi Electronics?

575
00:46:57,514 --> 00:47:00,420
[Oh Hyun Nam,
Durumi Electronics Sales Team 3]

576
00:47:11,565 --> 00:47:15,152
I put the advice you gave me to good use.

577
00:47:16,885 --> 00:47:18,937
The advice I gave you?

578
00:47:18,937 --> 00:47:20,637
Oh.

579
00:47:21,493 --> 00:47:23,518
How long have you two been dating?

580
00:47:24,209 --> 00:47:25,909
What?

581
00:47:26,881 --> 00:47:31,452
You didn't use it on some woman
you'd barely even met, did you?

582
00:47:35,165 --> 00:47:39,152
Good grief, only a lunatic would do that.

583
00:47:40,613 --> 00:47:42,313
Jeez.

584
00:47:53,261 --> 00:47:55,252
Do you have anything to say?

585
00:47:57,025 --> 00:47:59,918
I was just going to get something to drink.

586
00:48:00,629 --> 00:48:02,329
Okay.

587
00:48:10,305 --> 00:48:13,497
Excuse me, who... are you?

588
00:48:13,497 --> 00:48:15,425
Oh, my!

589
00:48:15,425 --> 00:48:17,625
Tae Min.

590
00:48:17,625 --> 00:48:19,041
Are you crazy?

591
00:48:19,041 --> 00:48:21,709
Are you dating someone?

592
00:48:21,709 --> 00:48:23,101
Hey!

593
00:48:23,101 --> 00:48:26,752
Wow, this is so unfamiliar. Very unfamiliar.

594
00:48:30,881 --> 00:48:32,985
Hey, this place has changed a little.

595
00:48:36,857 --> 00:48:38,685
Did you take a shower?

596
00:48:41,513 --> 00:48:43,213
Huh?

597
00:48:44,609 --> 00:48:46,752
And what's with your hair...

598
00:48:47,623 --> 00:48:49,323
Hey!

599
00:48:55,925 --> 00:48:57,297
Is everything all right now?

600
00:48:57,297 --> 00:48:59,129
Yeah.

601
00:48:59,129 --> 00:49:00,477
Yul's doing better now.

602
00:49:00,477 --> 00:49:03,852
No, I mean you.
You've never been like that before.

603
00:49:07,689 --> 00:49:09,389
Well...

604
00:49:11,325 --> 00:49:12,989
Maybe it's because I'm a mom now?

605
00:49:12,989 --> 00:49:15,118
If that's all it is, that's a relief.

606
00:49:16,452 --> 00:49:20,052
You.... Why did you follow me back then?

607
00:49:28,929 --> 00:49:31,052
Take me with you too.

608
00:49:32,145 --> 00:49:34,417
I didn't get my slingshot back then.

609
00:49:34,417 --> 00:49:37,305
When I came to Korea, why did you follow me?

610
00:49:37,305 --> 00:49:39,418
Because Yoo Bo Na was going.

611
00:49:42,225 --> 00:49:43,885
Then...

612
00:49:44,741 --> 00:49:47,085
if I leave again someday,

613
00:49:47,869 --> 00:49:49,885
will you follow me then too?

614
00:49:51,309 --> 00:49:53,009
Are you going somewhere?

615
00:50:01,241 --> 00:50:03,318
Where would I even go?

616
00:50:03,318 --> 00:50:05,252
Everything I need is right here.

617
00:50:08,185 --> 00:50:11,421
Any update on that punk?

618
00:50:11,421 --> 00:50:12,901
Nothing much.

619
00:50:12,901 --> 00:50:14,885
What's up? Is something happening?

620
00:50:23,837 --> 00:50:27,385
No. I guess I'm just being sensitive.

621
00:50:28,489 --> 00:50:31,385
Please check his main routes and let me know.

622
00:50:31,709 --> 00:50:33,749
[Chief's Office]

623
00:50:33,749 --> 00:50:37,589
What's gotten into you?
Why have you been so out of it lately?

624
00:50:37,589 --> 00:50:39,245
Is something going on?

625
00:50:39,245 --> 00:50:41,637
No. Nothing like that.

626
00:50:41,637 --> 00:50:43,833
That's the problem.

627
00:50:43,833 --> 00:50:46,233
Can you have nothing going on?
Of course, you can't.

628
00:50:46,233 --> 00:50:47,849
You should have plenty going on.

629
00:50:47,849 --> 00:50:50,752
It's been ages since the Kingfisher
task force was launched.

630
00:50:50,752 --> 00:50:52,917
You should have something
to show for it by now.

631
00:50:52,917 --> 00:50:55,441
Me? Show what?

632
00:50:55,441 --> 00:50:57,177
What do you mean, "what"?

633
00:50:57,177 --> 00:51:00,052
Who Kingfisher is, how old he is,
where he lives, what he does.

634
00:51:00,052 --> 00:51:01,665
Why should I?

635
00:51:01,665 --> 00:51:04,517
Why me? There are loads of reporters around.

636
00:51:04,517 --> 00:51:07,297
Why should I be the one doing that?

637
00:51:07,297 --> 00:51:12,218
You've devoted years to chasing Kingfisher.
Why are you getting mad?

638
00:51:16,245 --> 00:51:20,693
I hear this task force
is different from the previous ones.

639
00:51:20,693 --> 00:51:23,881
Everyone's closing in, thinking they
might actually get something this time.

640
00:51:23,881 --> 00:51:26,618
Do you want to end up doing nothing
but transcribing everyone else's work?

641
00:51:28,841 --> 00:51:32,261
Those Kingfisher articles
you've written over the years.

642
00:51:32,261 --> 00:51:36,537
They offer a different depth
and perspective. I like them!

643
00:51:36,537 --> 00:51:39,373
Honestly, your articles were pretty
sympathetic toward Kingfisher, weren't they?

644
00:51:39,373 --> 00:51:41,517
And you're just going to
sit on the sidelines now?

645
00:51:41,517 --> 00:51:45,785
You're really going to let everyone say
whatever they want about Kingfisher?

646
00:52:08,506 --> 00:52:09,461
[Kwon Tae Seong]

647
00:52:09,485 --> 00:52:11,596
[Kingfisher, Search Results]

648
00:52:13,974 --> 00:52:16,733
[If I Ever Meet Kingfisher]

649
00:52:21,615 --> 00:52:25,513
[If I Ever Meet Kingfisher]

650
00:52:29,665 --> 00:52:31,206
<i>What kind of person</i>

651
00:52:31,206 --> 00:52:34,485
<i>would devote their entire life
to something like that?</i>

652
00:52:36,353 --> 00:52:38,281
<i>But I didn't.</i>

653
00:52:38,281 --> 00:52:42,185
<i>I never carelessly speculated about him.</i>

654
00:52:42,185 --> 00:52:45,173
<i>So even if Kingfisher's identity
is revealed someday,</i>

655
00:52:45,173 --> 00:52:47,418
<i>I won't be surprised.</i>

656
00:52:48,037 --> 00:52:52,093
<i>I'll simply look forward to the day
I finally meet him.</i>

657
00:52:52,093 --> 00:52:55,552
<i>I want to sit beside him by the campfire</i>

658
00:52:55,552 --> 00:52:58,152
<i>and listen to him talk about
his life all night.</i>

659
00:52:58,913 --> 00:53:03,152
<i>Without asking anything,
I could simply listen.</i>

660
00:53:10,521 --> 00:53:14,585
<i>But if I were to meet him as
an ordinary citizen rather than a reporter,</i>

661
00:53:14,585 --> 00:53:18,997
<i>I'd have a legal duty
to report him to the police.</i>

662
00:53:18,997 --> 00:53:20,985
<i>Could I do that?</i>

663
00:53:21,852 --> 00:53:24,018
<i>Can I actually turn him in?</i>

664
00:53:24,985 --> 00:53:30,552
<i>To that question,
I haven't found an answer yet.</i>

665
00:53:30,552 --> 00:53:32,852
Will you report it to the police?

666
00:53:34,618 --> 00:53:39,685
Oh, since you're a reporter,
are you going to expose her in an article?

667
00:53:40,665 --> 00:53:43,718
Did you do that to me that day
because you were afraid I'd do that?

668
00:53:44,469 --> 00:53:48,252
If that was the case, I wouldn't
have just put you to sleep.

669
00:53:51,543 --> 00:53:55,493
Well, let's just say I changed my mind.

670
00:53:55,493 --> 00:53:56,733
Because I got curious.

671
00:53:56,733 --> 00:54:00,761
About what exactly Yoo Bo Na
is trying to protect.

672
00:54:00,761 --> 00:54:02,652
And whether she'll be

673
00:54:03,352 --> 00:54:06,485
able to keep protecting it.

674
00:54:06,485 --> 00:54:08,285
What do you mean?

675
00:54:08,285 --> 00:54:11,752
It's probably the same kind of thing?

676
00:54:11,752 --> 00:54:17,429
The reason you wanted to
keep your promise to me.

677
00:54:17,429 --> 00:54:21,718
Oh, by the way, Yoo Bo Na
doesn't know about that day, right?

678
00:54:21,718 --> 00:54:25,917
That's why I'm still alive and well.

679
00:54:25,917 --> 00:54:30,252
Isn't it probably the same thing?

680
00:54:30,252 --> 00:54:33,152
The reason why you had to

681
00:54:33,152 --> 00:54:37,085
remain in the dark about Yoo Bo Na.

682
00:54:39,818 --> 00:54:46,218
"What matters is the present, not the past."
You once said it, right?

683
00:54:47,318 --> 00:54:52,518
Yoo Bo Na was Yoo Bo Na in the past,
and she's still Yoo Bo Na now.

684
00:54:52,518 --> 00:54:56,201
What's left is your choice, isn't it?

685
00:54:56,201 --> 00:54:58,952
Whether you go with her or leave her behind.

686
00:54:58,952 --> 00:55:03,352
Including reporting or exposing her
in an article, of course.

687
00:55:08,294 --> 00:55:12,109
[Durumi Electronics]

688
00:55:24,649 --> 00:55:26,349
Ms. Oh Hyun Nam!

689
00:55:37,201 --> 00:55:39,552
Don't you want some coffee?

690
00:55:44,677 --> 00:55:46,061
<i>Oh, excuse me!</i>

691
00:55:46,061 --> 00:55:47,985
I think you dropped something.

692
00:55:48,785 --> 00:55:50,952
Thank you.

693
00:56:17,393 --> 00:56:19,505
Why's there nowhere to park around here?

694
00:56:19,505 --> 00:56:21,418
What, isn't it here?

695
00:56:22,777 --> 00:56:25,341
Kingfisher's hiatus...

696
00:56:25,341 --> 00:56:28,552
What were the exact dates again?

697
00:56:30,357 --> 00:56:31,629
Grandma!

698
00:56:31,629 --> 00:56:33,229
Oh, my, look who's here!

699
00:56:33,229 --> 00:56:35,252
Yul is here.

700
00:56:36,561 --> 00:56:38,352
- You're here?
- Yes, Mother.

701
00:56:38,352 --> 00:56:39,593
Did you just get off work?

702
00:56:39,593 --> 00:56:42,321
Yeah, Yul wanted your fried chicken,
so I brought her.

703
00:56:42,321 --> 00:56:44,549
- Oh.
- Really?

704
00:56:44,549 --> 00:56:47,345
I'll fry you some really tasty chicken.

705
00:56:47,345 --> 00:56:49,045
Okay.

706
00:56:50,121 --> 00:56:51,245
Come sit down.

707
00:56:51,245 --> 00:56:52,945
Yes, Mother.

708
00:56:54,245 --> 00:56:56,445
Oh, Tae Seong's coming too, right?

709
00:56:56,445 --> 00:56:59,865
Oh, he's been pretty busy lately, Mother.

710
00:56:59,865 --> 00:57:02,957
I barely even see him myself.

711
00:57:02,957 --> 00:57:04,752
Really?

712
00:57:05,845 --> 00:57:07,169
I'll have it ready in no time.

713
00:57:07,169 --> 00:57:09,897
She's being unusually sweet.

714
00:57:09,897 --> 00:57:12,318
Is this the power of money?

715
00:57:15,457 --> 00:57:17,717
Yul, tear it up and eat it.

716
00:57:17,717 --> 00:57:20,305
Are things hard for you these days?

717
00:57:20,305 --> 00:57:23,385
You look really tired and stressed out.

718
00:57:23,385 --> 00:57:25,118
Well...

719
00:57:29,452 --> 00:57:35,289
Mother, Tae Seong hasn't said
anything unusual to you, has he?

720
00:57:35,289 --> 00:57:38,618
He hasn't really told me anything...

721
00:57:39,421 --> 00:57:41,165
Why? What's up with Tae Seong?

722
00:57:41,165 --> 00:57:44,185
Is Tae Seong cheating on you?

723
00:57:45,561 --> 00:57:47,529
Be careful what you say around the kid.

724
00:57:47,529 --> 00:57:49,989
You think he'd do something like that?

725
00:57:49,989 --> 00:57:52,757
I'm just kidding!

726
00:57:52,757 --> 00:57:55,873
- Yul, eat plenty.
- Okay.

727
00:57:57,589 --> 00:57:59,793
I'm not too sure, Mother.

728
00:57:59,793 --> 00:58:04,785
I just feel like Tae Seong's been
a little upset with me lately.

729
00:58:05,645 --> 00:58:09,165
What could he be upset with you about?

730
00:58:09,165 --> 00:58:11,237
I guess that time has come.

731
00:58:11,237 --> 00:58:15,809
That's why I quit working
when Hyeok Jun was five.

732
00:58:15,809 --> 00:58:21,252
My husband made such a fuss about me
putting work before our child and him...

733
00:58:22,597 --> 00:58:24,617
Then quit your job too.

734
00:58:24,617 --> 00:58:25,937
Mom!

735
00:58:25,937 --> 00:58:27,585
You're not exactly saving the world.

736
00:58:27,585 --> 00:58:31,345
What could possibly be more important
to a woman than her husband and child?

737
00:58:31,345 --> 00:58:34,018
Oh, Bo Na, don't take it to heart.

738
00:58:35,625 --> 00:58:37,652
There's one thing.

739
00:58:39,045 --> 00:58:40,652
My own life.

740
00:58:40,652 --> 00:58:43,477
I got married at 24

741
00:58:43,477 --> 00:58:47,885
and lived only for my husband and kids.

742
00:58:47,885 --> 00:58:51,589
Then when Tae Seong's dad
suddenly passed away, I felt so lost.

743
00:58:51,589 --> 00:58:55,518
I needed to make a living,
but I didn't know how to do anything.

744
00:58:55,518 --> 00:58:59,109
So I scraped together what I had
and opened this place.

745
00:58:59,109 --> 00:59:02,518
At first, I was embarrassed
to be frying chicken.

746
00:59:02,518 --> 00:59:04,976
Oil splashed everywhere, my skin got burned,

747
00:59:04,976 --> 00:59:08,118
and I had to deal with drunk customers.

748
00:59:08,118 --> 00:59:09,885
Good grief.

749
00:59:11,341 --> 00:59:14,109
I cried a lot too.

750
00:59:14,109 --> 00:59:15,773
Mom.

751
00:59:15,773 --> 00:59:18,152
But I came back to the shop the next day.

752
00:59:18,152 --> 00:59:19,785
I had to open the doors.

753
00:59:19,785 --> 00:59:22,885
No matter how hard it was, I kept showing up.

754
00:59:22,885 --> 00:59:26,505
And you know what? I came to like it.

755
00:59:26,505 --> 00:59:29,569
I was the owner of this shop.

756
00:59:29,569 --> 00:59:32,273
Frying chicken was my job.

757
00:59:32,273 --> 00:59:37,285
I realized, "Oh, this is my life."

758
00:59:44,029 --> 00:59:46,981
Working while raising a child isn't easy.

759
00:59:46,981 --> 00:59:48,633
But what can you do?

760
00:59:48,633 --> 00:59:50,573
Unless you absolutely hate what you do,

761
00:59:50,573 --> 00:59:54,452
if it's something you love,
you have to see it through.

762
00:59:56,609 --> 00:59:58,501
Oh, I completely forgot.

763
00:59:58,501 --> 01:00:01,218
I left a dishcloth boiling on the stove.

764
01:00:03,525 --> 01:00:05,749
When you're both busy, bring Yul here.

765
01:00:05,749 --> 01:00:08,818
I'll watch her,
even if I have to close the shop.

766
01:00:10,725 --> 01:00:12,885
And pay me for the day's work.

767
01:00:14,349 --> 01:00:16,409
Didn't you say you'd never close up,
no matter what?

768
01:00:16,409 --> 01:00:18,518
You changed your tune pretty fast, huh?

769
01:00:26,885 --> 01:00:29,225
Mommy, catch me if you can!

770
01:00:29,225 --> 01:00:30,609
Yul!

771
01:00:30,609 --> 01:00:33,289
Oh, you're too fast. I can't catch you.

772
01:00:33,289 --> 01:00:34,552
- What should we do next then?
- Mommy!

773
01:00:34,552 --> 01:00:38,185
- I want to do that!
- Okay, go on up. You're good at that.

774
01:00:38,185 --> 01:00:40,418
Watch your head.

775
01:00:40,418 --> 01:00:42,618
Wow.

776
01:00:42,618 --> 01:00:44,365
Wow, you're good!

777
01:00:44,365 --> 01:00:48,269
I actually don't really like
strawberry shakes.

778
01:00:48,269 --> 01:00:52,705
But when I fell in love,
I really wanted to do that.

779
01:00:52,705 --> 01:00:55,421
Sitting across from each other
and drinking strawberry shakes.

780
01:00:55,421 --> 01:00:58,218
<i>Because that's the kind of
person you are to me.</i>

781
01:01:01,421 --> 01:01:03,485
You're going higher!

782
01:01:03,485 --> 01:01:05,441
Mommy, I want to do that.

783
01:01:05,441 --> 01:01:07,405
Okay.

784
01:01:07,405 --> 01:01:08,925
Can you get up on your own, Yul?

785
01:01:08,925 --> 01:01:11,025
- Yeah, I can get up.
- Go ahead. Stand up.

786
01:01:11,025 --> 01:01:13,805
Oh, let's see.

787
01:01:13,805 --> 01:01:15,605
Your hand looks okay. Right?

788
01:01:15,605 --> 01:01:19,185
Does it hurt? You're bleeding a little, Yul.

789
01:01:19,522 --> 01:01:20,235
[A Band-Aid]

790
01:01:22,785 --> 01:01:24,485
Does it hurt?

791
01:01:31,005 --> 01:01:33,852
With this on,
it'll get better in no time, right?

792
01:01:33,852 --> 01:01:35,552
Yeah.

793
01:01:37,353 --> 01:01:39,329
Wow, it really stuck on well.

794
01:01:39,329 --> 01:01:40,885
Did it stick?

795
01:01:40,885 --> 01:01:42,585
Yeah.

796
01:01:43,985 --> 01:01:45,857
Huh? It's Daddy!

797
01:01:45,857 --> 01:01:48,389
Daddy!

798
01:01:48,389 --> 01:01:50,577
My little precious!

799
01:01:50,577 --> 01:01:52,021
- Did you have fun?
- Yeah.

800
01:01:52,021 --> 01:01:53,285
What did you do?

801
01:01:53,285 --> 01:01:54,637
I went on the swings too.

802
01:01:54,637 --> 01:01:56,785
You're back early today.

803
01:01:56,785 --> 01:01:59,149
Yeah, I finished early.

804
01:01:59,149 --> 01:02:01,437
What about dinner?

805
01:02:01,437 --> 01:02:03,385
Well, not yet.

806
01:02:04,085 --> 01:02:05,933
Let's go home. I'll whip up
something tasty for you.

807
01:02:05,933 --> 01:02:07,633
Okay.

808
01:02:18,424 --> 01:02:20,180
Even right now, Kingfisher could be

809
01:02:20,180 --> 01:02:24,144
sitting at a dinner table
looking completely ordinary.

810
01:02:24,144 --> 01:02:29,868
A diligent employee,
someone's spouse, or a loving parent.

811
01:02:29,868 --> 01:02:34,245
He could've gotten married,
started a family, and had kids, like me.

812
01:02:34,245 --> 01:02:36,607
- Hey, you.
- Hey, who knows?

813
01:02:36,607 --> 01:02:39,560
That sticker might really have been a clue.

814
01:02:39,560 --> 01:02:41,780
<i>You never know.</i>

815
01:02:45,266 --> 01:02:46,476
[Headband, Red Devil, Tall and Slender]

816
01:02:46,504 --> 01:02:47,486
[Short or Tied Hair, Big Bag on Shoulder]

817
01:03:00,352 --> 01:03:02,113
Who is it?

818
01:03:18,048 --> 01:03:19,464
What brings you here at this hour,
out of the blue?

819
01:03:19,464 --> 01:03:22,513
I happened to be nearby,
so I stopped in to see Yul.

820
01:03:23,360 --> 01:03:25,812
Yul, Mr. Dong Jin is here!

821
01:03:25,812 --> 01:03:27,928
Mr. Lee!

822
01:03:27,928 --> 01:03:32,047
Oh, Yul. There's my Yul.

823
01:03:32,047 --> 01:03:35,032
Yul, how old are you?

824
01:03:35,032 --> 01:03:39,824
- Four.
- That's right, four.

825
01:03:39,824 --> 01:03:41,384
Dong Jin, you're here?

826
01:03:41,384 --> 01:03:42,784
Oh, yes.

827
01:03:42,784 --> 01:03:44,713
Sorry for dropping by without calling.

828
01:03:44,713 --> 01:03:47,512
- Not at all.
- I already had dinner.

829
01:03:47,512 --> 01:03:50,280
Grab some tea and fruit. Come on in.

830
01:04:10,728 --> 01:04:13,800
Why are you just standing there? Sit down.

831
01:04:13,800 --> 01:04:18,052
- When did you say you first met Bo Na?
- Huh?

832
01:04:18,052 --> 01:04:19,763
Eight years ago, during the World Cup.

833
01:04:19,763 --> 01:04:22,452
When you had your head cracked open
and were in the hospital, right?

834
01:04:22,452 --> 01:04:25,440
Why are you suddenly
asking about my love life?

835
01:04:25,440 --> 01:04:27,644
Are you lonely these days?

836
01:04:27,644 --> 01:04:29,680
Mr. Lee, look at this.

837
01:04:30,520 --> 01:04:32,684
Oh, Yul!

838
01:04:32,684 --> 01:04:36,093
Wow, you put stickers on your doll?

839
01:04:36,093 --> 01:04:37,747
Wow.

840
01:04:42,676 --> 01:04:45,424
It's a Baby Shark sticker!

841
01:04:45,424 --> 01:04:47,780
You like Baby Shark, don't you, Yul?

842
01:04:47,780 --> 01:04:49,580
Yeah, I do.

843
01:04:50,580 --> 01:04:53,248
Come on, what kid doesn't
like that these days?

844
01:04:53,248 --> 01:04:57,560
Just like you said, every home in the country
with a toddler has tons of them.

845
01:04:57,560 --> 01:04:59,260
Yeah.

846
01:05:00,112 --> 01:05:01,928
Dong Jin, have some fruit.

847
01:05:01,928 --> 01:05:03,628
Oh, thank you.

848
01:05:09,992 --> 01:05:11,536
Are you still busy these days?

849
01:05:11,536 --> 01:05:12,876
Well, yes.

850
01:05:12,876 --> 01:05:16,313
I joined the Kingfisher task force.

851
01:05:16,313 --> 01:05:18,813
Oh, then you must be really busy.

852
01:05:18,813 --> 01:05:20,720
Well, it's just...

853
01:05:20,720 --> 01:05:24,620
You returned to work after taking
three years of parental leave, right?

854
01:05:24,620 --> 01:05:26,700
Have you adjusted okay?

855
01:05:26,700 --> 01:05:29,732
Well, yeah. Everything's fine.

856
01:05:29,732 --> 01:05:33,913
She's been back at work for ages.
Mind your own business, man.

857
01:05:37,432 --> 01:05:40,547
Well, you know Gu Jong Ryeol, right?

858
01:05:41,296 --> 01:05:42,660
Gu Jong Ryeol?

859
01:05:42,660 --> 01:05:45,044
- Yeah.
- Oh, yeah.

860
01:05:45,044 --> 01:05:46,768
I saw the article.

861
01:05:46,768 --> 01:05:48,513
I have a feeling...

862
01:05:49,268 --> 01:05:52,013
that it was the work of Kingfisher.

863
01:05:55,424 --> 01:05:58,780
Yul, do you want some fruit?

864
01:06:00,640 --> 01:06:02,340
Here you go.

865
01:06:03,347 --> 01:06:06,913
There were severe signs of
blunt-force trauma on his face.

866
01:06:06,913 --> 01:06:10,600
But Kingfisher has never physically
touched his victims before.

867
01:06:10,600 --> 01:06:13,700
You know him better than anyone.
You're the Kingfisher expert.

868
01:06:13,700 --> 01:06:15,664
What are you doing talking about work here?

869
01:06:15,664 --> 01:06:17,304
Have some fruit. It's good.

870
01:06:17,304 --> 01:06:19,400
Alright.

871
01:06:19,400 --> 01:06:23,304
The profiler said there was emotion involved.

872
01:06:23,304 --> 01:06:27,880
If he beat him that brutally,
there had to be anger behind it.

873
01:06:28,847 --> 01:06:31,460
The kid can hear you. Stop.

874
01:06:31,460 --> 01:06:33,347
Well, it just made me

875
01:06:33,960 --> 01:06:36,180
think of something.

876
01:06:37,247 --> 01:06:41,747
Could Kingfisher be a parent raising a child?

877
01:06:43,613 --> 01:06:45,352
Mommy, have one of these.

878
01:06:45,352 --> 01:06:47,052
Okay.

879
01:06:48,772 --> 01:06:51,276
Yul, do you like apples better?

880
01:06:51,276 --> 01:06:52,752
You said it yourself.

881
01:06:52,752 --> 01:06:56,147
He could've gotten married and had a child.
You never know.

882
01:06:58,156 --> 01:06:59,948
Finished your tea?

883
01:06:59,948 --> 01:07:01,780
Let's step outside.

884
01:07:09,896 --> 01:07:12,047
Do you have something to say to me?

885
01:07:12,980 --> 01:07:15,480
Say it. Stop beating around the bush.
What is it?

886
01:07:18,484 --> 01:07:20,680
Are you in league with Kingfisher?

887
01:07:22,836 --> 01:07:26,213
What kind of nonsense
have you been spouting lately?

888
01:07:26,213 --> 01:07:29,880
The person you said you had to
protect with that embargo,

889
01:07:30,892 --> 01:07:32,592
is it Kingfisher?

890
01:07:35,072 --> 01:07:39,732
<i>To that question,
I haven't found an answer yet.</i>

891
01:07:39,732 --> 01:07:43,113
No, I'm on your side.

892
01:07:46,816 --> 01:07:48,906
I'm being serious.

893
01:07:48,906 --> 01:07:53,232
That man I saw before,
he really is Kingfisher.

894
01:07:53,232 --> 01:07:54,628
On the day of the Haegong-dong incident,

895
01:07:54,628 --> 01:07:57,948
I tailed Yeon Chang Bok's mom
and found where Yeon Chang Bok was hiding.

896
01:07:57,948 --> 01:08:01,864
I searched the nearby rooftops, spotted
Kingfisher taking aim, and got caught.

897
01:08:01,864 --> 01:08:04,668
Hey, why are you only telling me this now?

898
01:08:04,668 --> 01:08:07,680
Because he threatened to harm my family.

899
01:08:08,316 --> 01:08:12,213
Then the person you said
you had to protect....

900
01:08:12,213 --> 01:08:15,980
My wife and my child. My beloved family.

901
01:08:16,900 --> 01:08:18,680
I need to protect them.

902
01:08:23,204 --> 01:08:25,013
You'll be on my side, right?

903
01:08:25,740 --> 01:08:27,612
Huh?

904
01:08:27,612 --> 01:08:29,680
You said you wanted to repay the favor.

905
01:08:49,104 --> 01:08:50,856
Did you see him off okay?

906
01:08:50,856 --> 01:08:53,280
Yul fell asleep.

907
01:08:54,820 --> 01:08:57,747
I'll clean up. You go wash up first, honey.

908
01:09:07,956 --> 01:09:09,656
What's wrong?

909
01:09:25,832 --> 01:09:30,580
I'm done with everything busy now.
Want to take Yul out this weekend?

910
01:09:34,812 --> 01:09:36,512
I'd love to.

911
01:10:01,476 --> 01:10:03,772
Yul, look at Daddy.

912
01:10:03,772 --> 01:10:05,472
Daddy!

913
01:10:06,716 --> 01:10:08,513
Look at Daddy.

914
01:10:23,192 --> 01:10:25,247
Mommy, hello!

915
01:10:27,788 --> 01:10:29,488
Be careful!

916
01:10:31,548 --> 01:10:33,248
Got you.

917
01:10:39,052 --> 01:10:41,880
Mommy's taking a picture! Look at Mommy!

918
01:10:45,016 --> 01:10:46,716
Yul!

919
01:10:58,576 --> 01:11:00,694
- Oh, dear...
- Sir, let me help you with that.

920
01:11:00,694 --> 01:11:03,294
Oh... Yes. Thank you.

921
01:11:13,516 --> 01:11:15,672
It's super yummy.

922
01:11:15,672 --> 01:11:17,488
- I love you.
- You love Mommy?

923
01:11:17,488 --> 01:11:18,488
I love you too.

924
01:11:18,488 --> 01:11:20,188
I love you too.

925
01:11:26,224 --> 01:11:27,547
Oh, thank you.

926
01:11:27,547 --> 01:11:29,480
- Yes.
- Thank you.

927
01:11:42,080 --> 01:11:43,813
Wait...

928
01:11:45,224 --> 01:11:47,347
Call an ambulance!

929
01:11:47,347 --> 01:11:49,047
What happened?

930
01:13:11,057 --> 01:13:15,206
[A Bona Fide Killer]

931
01:13:15,380 --> 01:13:17,936
What exactly is the point of all this?

932
01:13:17,936 --> 01:13:19,880
Kingfisher's social death?

933
01:13:19,880 --> 01:13:21,800
Is Kingfisher seriously insane?

934
01:13:21,800 --> 01:13:24,420
Why would he suddenly start killing people
who aren't even criminals?

935
01:13:24,420 --> 01:13:27,208
Isn't it possible the killer
isn't Kingfisher?

936
01:13:27,208 --> 01:13:28,613
Do you have evidence?

937
01:13:28,613 --> 01:13:30,032
We'll need to check that out from now on.

938
01:13:30,032 --> 01:13:34,076
Someone who can imitate Kingfisher
and wants to bring him down.

939
01:13:34,076 --> 01:13:35,800
Bo Na, I can't find Yul!

940
01:13:35,800 --> 01:13:37,940
We have to catch them
before there's a third victim.

941
01:13:37,940 --> 01:13:41,200
I heard hair with matching DNA
was found at both shooting locations.

942
01:13:41,200 --> 01:13:42,913
We found it.
